Package: screen-recorder
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Section: video
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Screen Recorder <screen-recorder@localhost>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.11), python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-adw-1 (>= 1.5), gir1.2-gstreamer-1.0, gstreamer1.0-pipewire, gstreamer1.0-pulseaudio, gstreamer1.0-plugins-base, gstreamer1.0-plugins-good, gstreamer1.0-plugins-bad, gstreamer1.0-plugins-ugly, gstreamer1.0-libav, pipewire, pipewire-pulse | pulseaudio, xdg-desktop-portal, xdg-desktop-portal-gnome | xdg-desktop-portal-backend
Recommends: gstreamer1.0-vaapi, intel-media-va-driver | mesa-va-drivers, ffmpeg
Description: Record the screen and audio to MP4
 A small GTK application that records one monitor together with the
 microphone and desktop sound into a crash-safe H.264/AAC MP4 file.
 Works on GNOME under Wayland and X11, uses hardware video encoding when
 available, and watches free disk space during long recordings.
